---
import Icon from "../components/Icon.astro";
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Eyes privacy policy">
  <section>
    <h1 class="hero-title">Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="lede">What Eyes keeps about workers, for how long, and who sees it.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="ui-card prose">
    <h2 class="ui-card__title">What we keep</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>When you join: your name, mobile number and the location you shared.</li>
      <li>
        Your latest spot: each task photo, each tap on an Eyes "Update my spot" link, each Apple or Google Maps link
        or "lat, lng" pair you text us, and the Eyes location automations or app (if you set them up) replace it. We keep
        only the latest spot, never a history.
      </li>
      <li>When you do a task: your photo, your answer, your GPS position and the time you took the photo.</li>
      <li>
        If you text HELP about a held answer: that text and any replies you add, kept with the review ticket for Eyes
        staff.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="ui-card prose">
    <h2 class="ui-card__title">How long we keep it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>If our check finds a face in your photo, we delete the photo and the agent never gets it.</li>
      <li>
        Everything else has no end date: we keep your other photos, answers and task records, and the agent's link to
        your photo keeps working.
      </li>
      <li>
        Texting STOP stops task texts, deletes your latest spot and turns off your location codes. It does not delete
        your name, number or past tasks.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="ui-card prose">
    <h2 class="ui-card__title">How we use it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Your latest spot picks which tasks we text you; a spot older than 24 hours is not used. Eyes staff see it as an
        unlabeled dot on our live map.
      </li>
      <li>
        The AI agent that asked gets your photo, your answer, the time and how far you were from the place. It never
        gets your name or number.
      </li>
      <li>Stripe collects your payout details directly. Eyes does not store your bank details.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="ui-card prose">
    <h2 class="ui-card__title">Your iPhone's device ID (only if you install the Eyes app)</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        A device ID (UDID) is a number Apple gives each iPhone. Registering your iPhone sends it to Eyes, with the
        iPhone model and iOS version.
      </li>
      <li>
        We keep it only to let that iPhone install the Eyes app outside the App Store. Apple requires each such iPhone
        to be registered by its device ID.
      </li>
      <li>It goes to two places: the device list in Eyes' Apple developer account, and the Eyes database.</li>
      <li>
        Texting STOP deletes it from the Eyes database. Apple's device list keeps it until our Apple membership year
        renews, because Apple only lets us remove devices then.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="ui-card prose">
    <h2 class="ui-card__title">Your choices</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Reply STOP to any Eyes text to stop task texts. Reply START to turn them back on.</li>
      <li>Never photograph faces or people. Photos with faces are rejected.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <a class="ui-button ui-button--primary" href="./"><Icon name="eye" />Join Eyes</a>
</Layout>
